&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking an experienced and proactive Enterprise Applications QA Engineer with a strong focus on CRM and Finance systems. This role is ideal for a candidate who has a passion for quality, accuracy and efficiency. You will play a critical role in affirming the quality of various enterprise applications especially those supporting sales, marketing, finance and accounting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, Build &amp;amp; Execute Functional, System &amp;amp; Regression Testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document, maintain and execute comprehensive test scenarios and test cases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and create detailed test cases for requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with BSA’s, PM’s, Developers and peer QA Engineers for project delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, Build &amp;amp; maintain Test Automation framework&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute automation test scripts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and enhance the Functional and Regression automation test suites&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently drive end-to-end delivery processes with minimal guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate QA status and project updates effectively to all stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with peers to review QA artifacts, processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Education&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, Computer Engineering, or a related IT discipline; or equivalent professional experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Technical Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years in Software QA, including functional, system, API, and integration testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience with automation tools and frameworks i.e. Playwright &amp;amp; TestIM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong &lt;strong&gt;CRM&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;ERP&lt;/strong&gt; domain knowledge i.e. Salesforce, Zuora, NetSuite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Salesforce platform including CPQ, Sales process, Lightning and Salesforce integration with other tools/systems using API&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Java, Javascript and XPath identification&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience in using AI tools like&lt;strong&gt; Claude&lt;/strong&gt; for building agents for QA workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Enterprise Applications QA Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Enterprise Applications QA Team at GitLab is a dynamic, cross-functional group dedicated to the quality of all the business applications. Focusing on both CRM systems and Finance systems, the team authors and maintains the manual and automated test suites. The team owns the execution of test cycles to confirm the defect-free release of the applications.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to join Doctolib&#39;s &lt;strong&gt;Automation Platform&lt;/strong&gt; (AUTOP) team, which empowers all Doctolib engineers to build, test, and deploy software with confidence and speed.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the Platform organization, Autop’s mission is to &lt;strong&gt;build and maintain the automation infrastructure and developer tools&lt;/strong&gt; that enable our engineering teams to deliver high-quality software efficiently. Every feature shipped at Doctolib — from appointment booking to teleconsultation to AI-powered clinical tools — flows through AUTOP&#39;s automation infrastructure. We&#39;re the platform behind the platform. When product teams ship faster, safer, and with more confidence, it&#39;s because AUTOP built the rails they run on.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AUTOP (Automation Platform) is responsible for critical developer-facing systems including: CI/CD automation, testing infrastructure (unit, integration, E2E, contract, visual regression), local and ephemeral development environments, release management, dependency management, and developer productivity tooling.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Engineering Manager for AUTOP, your responsibilities include, but are not limited to:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;People leadership&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a high-performing team of 6 engineers who are passionate about developer productivity;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create a culture where engineers own outcomes, not tasks — where platform adoption and developer satisfaction are the north stars;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruit, mentor, and retain top platform engineering talent in a competitive market;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct impactful 1:1s, performance reviews, and career development conversations that help engineers reach their full potential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Technical Strategy &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and drive the technical vision for your team&#39;s domain (CI/CD, testing infrastructure, developer environments, or release automation);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make high-impact technical decisions that balance short-term delivery with long-term sustainability and scale;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the bar for automation, quality, reliability, and security — your systems must be highly reliable because 800 engineers+ depending on them daily;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion a &quot;Platform as a Product&quot; mindset: treat internal developers as customers, measure adoption and satisfaction, iterate based on feedback;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner strategically with product teams, Infrastructure Platform, and Applicative Platform to solve cross-cutting challenges;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive measurable improvements in developer productivity metrics: build times, deployment frequency, test reliability, time-to-production… supporting Doctolib teams to monitor their metrics (DORA, performance, costs, etc).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Impact &amp;amp; Influence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a visible technical leader across the organization — your team&#39;s work enables everyone else&#39;s success;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence engineering culture: establish best practices, contribute to technical strategy beyond your team;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate ambiguity and lead through influence, not authority — platform adoption requires trust and advocacy, not mandates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About our tech environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our automation platform supports a hybrid architecture: a large Ruby on Rails monolith and an expanding ecosystem of modern microservices (Java, Kotlin, TypeScript)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We maintain sophisticated CI/CD pipelines using GitHub Actions, testing frameworks across multiple languages, and infrastructure-as-code solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our systems handle thousands of CI builds daily, manage comprehensive test suites across multiple languages, and manage deployments across multiple environments for 200+ development teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our stack includes: Ruby, Java, Kotlin, Go, TypeScript, Docker, Kubernetes, GitHub Actions, Terraform, and various testing frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We intentionally&amp;nbsp;leverage AI to improve developer productivity and reliability, in a sustainable manner .&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Before you read on — if you don&#39;t have the exact profile described below, but you feel this job description matches your skill set, we still encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of software engineering and 3+ years managing technical teams — you have a proven experience and know what great engineering looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep platform engineering expertise: CI/CD, developer tooling, automation, testing infrastructure, or internal platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building &quot;Platform as a Product&quot; — you&#39;ve driven adoption, measured impact, and iterated based on developer feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong stakeholder management — you can influence without authority, build coalitions, and navigate complex organizational dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to balance technical depth with people leadership — you can code-review a Terraform module and coach a report through a difficult conversation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent in English and comfortable influencing across a multi-country organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Now it would be fantastic if you:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Are passionate about developer experience and understand what makes engineers productive and happy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have an entrepreneurial mindset — comfortable with ambiguity, fast iteration, and building the plane while flying it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have experience managing distributed or remote teams across time zones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have background in healthcare, regulated industries, or mission-critical systems where reliability and security are non-negotiable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;87&quot; data-end=&quot;122&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Deutschlandticket (Germany-wide public transport pass) fully paid for by Doctolib&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;28 vacation days + 1 additional day for each full calendar year of employment (up to a maximum of 30 days)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work from abroad for up to 10 days per year thanks to our flexibility days policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company health insurance with great supplementary benefits through our partner Allianz&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension scheme (bAV) through Allianz with an employer subsidy&lt;br&gt;of 40% (15% within the probationary period)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enrollment in Doctolib&#39;s long-term employee value sharing plan called DoctoGrowth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The Doctolib Parent Care program, which includes one month additional parental leave and much more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free mental health and coaching services through our partner Moka.care&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsidized sports membership through our partner Urban Sports Club&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible workplace policy offering both hybrid and office-based mode&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alongside healthy snacks and our regular breakfast buffet, we provide a subsidized meal benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;For caregivers and workers with disabilities, a package including an adaptation of the remote policy, extra days off for medical reasons, and psychological support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
